    <h3>Part 3: statRoll() — Generate a Single D&D-Style RPG Stat</h3>

    <p>
        In many RPGs, character stats are generated by rolling 3 six-sided dice
        (3d6) and summing the results. Build a method that does this.
    </p>

    <p><strong>Requirements:</strong></p>
    <ul>
        <li>Method signature: <code>public static int statRoll()</code></li>
        <li>Generates three d6 rolls and returns the sum</li>
        <li>This is a <em>convenience method</em> — it should call the
            <code>roll()</code> method you already wrote, not repeat the
            Math.random() logic.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic Checkpoint</h3>
        <p>
            Why call <code>roll(6)</code> three times instead of writing
            <code>(int)(Math.random() * 6) + 1</code> three times?
            What happens if you later discover a bug in your random formula —
            how many places would you need to fix?
        </p>
    </div>

    <p><strong>Acceptance Test:</strong></p>
    <pre><code>for (int i = 0; i &lt; 6; i++) {
    System.out.println("Stat " + (i+1) + ": " + Dice.statRoll());
}</code></pre>
    <p>Expected: six numbers, each between 3 and 18.</p>

    <div class="tinker">
        <h3>Tinker: d20 Check</h3>
        <p>
            RPGs also use d20 ability checks. Add a method:
        </p>
        <p><code>public static int d20Check()</code></p>
        <p>
            This rolls a d20 and prints whether it's:
            Natural 20 (critical success), Natural 1 (critical failure), or just
            a normal number. You'll need an <code>if/else</code> chain.
        </p>
